    },
    {
      "source": "DeFiHackLabs explorer",
      "text": "The root cause is in Staking Contract, the harvest() mishandling the rewardPerShare Code Snippet: Attack Tx: https://etherscan.io/tx/0xc9b2cbc1437bbcd8c328b6d7cdbdae33d7d2a9ef07eca18b4922aac0430991e7 Analysis:"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "On 9 March 2024, Juice Finance’s staking contract on Ethereum Mainnet was exploited due to a reward logic flaw, allowing an attacker to drain over 1.3 million JUICE tokens. These were sold for approximately 54 ETH ($54,000). The attacker used multiple transactions to extract tokens from the contract, with no evidence of funds recovery. The vulnerable staking contract failed to correctly account for rewards and token balances, enabling an attacker to harvest unearned JUICE tokens and drain both the liquidity pool and user stakes."
    }
